WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 1 Student Video
Unit 1, Lesson 1: Apologetics

1
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.140
There are answers to our questions.

2
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.080
From

3
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.660
the simplest things that pass through our consciousness to

4
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.070
the big questions about life and faith.

5
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.380
The word apologetics comes from the Greek word apologia, which can be translated as

6
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:49.140
answer. It means to give a reason, a defense, or an answer for what we believe

7
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.420
and why we believe it. When I was in college, I went to a friend's wedding and had

8
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.840
to fly home alone. I got to the airport in the morning and learned that my flight

9
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.080
was delayed about three or four hours.

10
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.520
So I turned around to go wait and I saw another young man about my age.

11
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.860
He was in college and I thought, you know what?

12
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.560
Here's an opportunity to go talk with him and maybe share my faith.

13
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.280
But then my next thought was, you know what?

14
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:22.000
I am really tired. God, if you want me to share with him, he's gonna have to sit by

15
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.220
me on the plane. I finally boarded the plane and I sat. A

16
00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.880
few moments later, I saw this young man walking down the aisle.

17
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.660
And of course, I'm wondering where he's gonna sit.

18
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.280
And he sits right next to me in 9B.

19
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.820
Whether this was a sign from God or not, it certainly was an opportunity.

20
00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.780
So I introduced myself, struck up a conversation, and eventually the topic turned

21
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.360
towards spiritual things. He asked me what I believe.

22
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.400
I said, I'm a Christian. I believe in Jesus.

23
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.480
He said, if you're a Christian, does that mean you think that the Bible is true?

24
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.880
And it's the word of God? I said, yes.

25
00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.540
He looked at me point blank. I'll never forget it.

26
00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.120
He said, how do you really know the Bible's true?

27
00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.980
And although my parents had trained me to give an answer, for some reason in this

28
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.420
circumstance, I fumbled around. And to be honest with you, I gave an answer that was

29
00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.560
really weak.

30
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.880
I walked away from that encounter a little bit upset and frustrated that I didn't

31
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.540
have a better response. And I remember thinking, next time, I'm gonna have a better

32
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.680
answer. In fact, I remember... I remember having a resolve that said, if God gives

33
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.580
me the chance to be in significant spiritual conversations again, I'm gonna have a

34
00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.940
good reason for why I believe in Christianity, and specifically, why I think the

35
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.700
Bible is true.

36
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:44.400
In 1 Peter 3:15, the Apostle Peter says to put Christ first in our

37
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.420
life, but then to be ready with an answer for the hope within, and to give it with

38
00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:52.920
gentleness, and to give it with respect towards other people.

39
00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.460
What's fascinating to me about this, is that it's not just about the Bible.

40
00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:58.180
What's fascinating to me about this passage is the pattern in which Peter says to

41
00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.600
first make Christ Lord of your life, and then be ready with an answer.

42
00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.660
Sometimes we flip this around. Sometimes we want to be ready with an answer before

43
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.540
we've really submitted our lives to Christ.

44
00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.420
And when that happens, oftentimes the results can be harmful.

45
00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.900
But when we first find our identity in Christ, and we experience His forgiveness,

46
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.840
and then we do apologetics out of a spirit of love, it can make a powerful

47
00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:31.700
difference in somebody's life. Being an apologist is not a spiritual gift,

48
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.680
like wisdom, discernment, or teaching.

49
00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.480
Being an apologist is not just for pastors, teachers, parents, and professors.

50
00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.460
We are all called to be ready with an answer for the hope within.

51
00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:50.200
I think C.S. Lewis is right. The question is not if we will be apologists, but how

52
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.060
good of an apologist will each of us be.

53
00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.140
Apology is not just about being an apologist.

54
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.440
Apologetics has been a staple of the Christian faith since its inception.

55
00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:03.380
Jesus was a kind of apologist. And the first followers of Jesus that came after the

56
00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:08.840
apostles, many of them were called apologists because they gave positive evidences

57
00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:12.580
for the Christian faith and responded to objections against it.

58
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.680
How much have you thought about why you believe as you believe?

59
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.680
Are you ready with an answer when someone asks you why you think the Bible is true?

60
00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.600
Have you thought through why if God is all good and all powerful, he allows evil?

61
00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:30.640
And have you thought through a response when people say that science conflicts with

62
00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.460
faith? And just as importantly, are you ready to share that answer with others when

63
00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.220
they ask you the reason for the hope within?

64
00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.740
We are called as Christians to be ready to make a case for the Christian faith.

65
00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.380
We're called to put forth arguments for what we believe.

66
00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.360
Now don't confuse that with being argumentative.

67
00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:55.080
That's a very different thing. We are not called to be divisive in how we treat

68
00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:59.600
people. But each of us are called to be ready with an answer for the hope within.

69
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.500
And that's exactly what we're going to do in this Bible study.

70
00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.420
I'm going to help you develop your convictions that Christianity is true and also

71
00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.800
have the confidence to share that faith with others.

72
00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:16.520
And just remember this, we are called to boldly speak truth, but we are to always do

73
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.760
it in love.

